WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.590
KK Ep 4 – Script

00:18.060 --> 00:20.390
If you turn me into a cyborg

00:18.060 --> 00:20.390
Kaizou suru nara

00:20.600 --> 00:23.060
install a self-destruct device

00:20.600 --> 00:23.060
Jibaku souchi wa

00:23.230 --> 00:26.770
as an option

00:23.230 --> 00:26.770
opshon tsukete kure

00:28.440 --> 00:29.570
If I

00:28.440 --> 00:29.570
Kimi o

00:29.740 --> 00:32.160
can't protect you

00:29.740 --> 00:32.160
Mamotte yarenai nara

00:32.320 --> 00:33.450
living

00:32.320 --> 00:33.450
Ikiteru

00:33.620 --> 00:34.740
has no meaning

00:33.620 --> 00:34.740
imi nai

00:34.910 --> 00:37.660
at all to me

00:34.910 --> 00:37.660
ore na no dakara

00:38.620 --> 00:41.080
Even if I had my erased memories back

00:38.620 --> 00:41.080
Kesareta kioku ni sae mo

00:41.210 --> 00:43.670
I wouldn't remember the two of us

00:41.210 --> 00:43.670
futari no omoide nai

00:43.920 --> 00:48.590
That's my one-sided and self-destructive love

00:43.920 --> 00:48.590
Sou wansaido jibaku no aisa

00:49.590 --> 00:51.550
I am still young

00:49.590 --> 00:51.550
Atara wakai

00:51.720 --> 00:55.010
but willing to exchange my life for yours

00:51.720 --> 00:55.010
Inochi o hikikaeshita tote kamawanai

00:56.180 --> 00:57.810
I'll become

00:56.180 --> 00:57.810
Kimi no

00:58.390 --> 01:00.060
your hero

00:58.390 --> 01:00.060
hiiroo ni naru

01:00.350 --> 01:02.640
If you are

01:00.350 --> 01:02.640
kimi ga akutou de

01:02.850 --> 01:07.020
kidnapped by villains

01:02.850 --> 01:07.020
saratte kureta nara

01:07.400 --> 01:11.440
You can upgrade me as you please

01:07.400 --> 01:11.440
katte ni kaizou shite mo ii ze

01:11.860 --> 01:15.450
[Elesa-Suimasen] presents

01:12.320 --> 01:15.450
Katte Ni

01:12.320 --> 01:15.450
Kaizou

01:15.870 --> 01:20.700
Second year student of Torauma High School, Katsu Kaizō is a cyborg.

01:20.700 --> 01:24.460
Attacked by mysterious people and left close to death with severe injuries

01:24.460 --> 01:27.590
he was turned into a cyborg by genius scientist Saien Suzu

01:27.590 --> 01:29.880
which saved his life.

01:29.880 --> 01:32.260
She brought along with her the underling Tsubouchi Chitan

01:32.260 --> 01:35.050
along with whom Kaizō continues his fight.

01:36.010 --> 01:39.510
Or at least, this is what he imagines.

01:44.620 --> 01:46.260
This is a game about limits.

01:46.720 --> 01:50.450
If the criminals love limits, they should show themselves for sure.

01:51.380 --> 01:52.850
Your turn, Umi-chan.

01:54.670 --> 01:56.170
I don't think they'll come for this...

01:58.380 --> 01:59.640
They really came!

01:59.640 --> 02:00.800
It's the limit!

02:00.800 --> 02:01.900
It really is the limit!

02:02.200 --> 02:06.480
It was you guys, right? You're the ones responsible for all these limit-incidents...

02:09.310 --> 02:11.680
Why are you pushing people to their limits?

02:11.680 --> 02:14.330
Isn't it better to leave some room and be safe?

02:14.790 --> 02:19.020
We used to think that safety was better, too.

02:19.210 --> 02:20.400
Then why...?

02:20.420 --> 02:23.360
Because Japan's myth of safety has collapsed!

02:23.390 --> 02:25.880
You're knocked down in a safety zone

02:26.250 --> 02:28.580
get cut with a safety razor

02:29.080 --> 02:31.500
Successful Applicant Announcement

02:29.100 --> 02:31.500
fail to get into your "safety school"

02:31.850 --> 02:34.240
and get punched with safety shoes!

02:34.720 --> 02:37.510
For the harmonious idiots that are today's Japanese

02:37.510 --> 02:39.990
it's necessary to be nervous about your limits!

02:40.330 --> 02:44.550
How stupid! Why do you need to push your limits on purpose?!

02:44.550 --> 02:46.980
Isn't it better to just be safe?!

02:47.000 --> 02:47.480
What!

02:47.590 --> 02:49.290
so are you one of the safety obsessed, too?

02:49.290 --> 02:50.790
A safety idealogue!!?

02:50.960 --> 02:55.210
Is this a safe day!?

02:55.790 --> 02:57.920
NO! Today is not a safe day!

02:58.030 --> 02:59.290
So you check them.

02:59.290 --> 03:00.950
Even though you don't need to.

03:01.490 --> 03:04.210
What's safe about Umi?

03:04.840 --> 03:06.920
We don't need such a limited heroine!

03:07.160 --> 03:10.930
Look at these Heroine-levels, she's way past the limits!

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Moé-Moé Level

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
To●Heart Level

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Reader Popularity
Level

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Actually, We Really Don't Need
Her At This Point Level

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Heart-throb Level

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Yamada-san

03:08.010 --> 03:10.930
Umi

03:11.290 --> 03:13.600
<b>Just what do you mean by that?!</b>

03:15.810 --> 03:19.710
Oh- Master, if you look closely at him... Isn't that Katsu Kaizō?

03:19.950 --> 03:23.810
He's the guy who pricked us with safety pins and ran us over in the safety zone!

03:24.160 --> 03:27.550
More perverts you've created again!?

03:28.590 --> 03:29.250
Well, it's all right...

03:29.560 --> 03:33.860
Thanks to you our eyes were opened to how wonderful limits are.

03:37.260 --> 03:39.070
A smile with margin?

03:39.220 --> 03:42.370
D... Don't rudely say that it has margin!

03:42.630 --> 03:44.530
We're always at our very limits!

03:45.430 --> 03:45.770
Well then...

03:46.570 --> 03:48.110
show me a smile at its limits.

03:49.890 --> 03:51.680
A smile... at its limits...

03:55.100 --> 03:56.970
How is that at its limits?

03:57.290 --> 04:03.630
Your limits seem to be like recording 121 minutes on a 120 minute tape.

04:04.200 --> 04:06.040
W-what did you just say!?

04:06.710 --> 04:09.030
So that's not close to the limit?

04:09.360 --> 04:13.560
There's roughly three extra minutes on a 120 minute tape.

04:14.210 --> 04:16.070
You should at least try for 3 times as much

04:16.070 --> 04:19.770
like recording a 15 episode anime on one tape!

04:20.040 --> 04:21.740
Stop talking like a maniac!

04:22.180 --> 04:25.570
A <i>good</i> example of a laugh at its limits is...

04:31.690 --> 04:34.820
That's right! That's it! A laugh at its limits!

04:35.080 --> 04:37.090
What is this bizarre, terrifying voice

04:37.090 --> 04:38.670
it sounds as if it's not even of this world!

04:39.660 --> 04:41.480
I'm scared, Master!

04:50.670 --> 04:52.890
He's...at the limits of being human...!

04:56.880 --> 05:01.600
I'm scared, please don't come near me!!

05:01.600 --> 05:03.850
Chitan-kun, are you about to blow your fuse again?

05:04.150 --> 05:07.460
I'm going on a journey to the limits, so I've got no margin left!

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
Route 1: Departure 19:27, Arrival 00:37. Time: 5:10 (3:47 by train, 1:23 by others)

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
Fares: 5,310 Yen (Train fees: 4,100 Yen, special fees: 1,210 Yen)

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
Tachikawa (weather at 21 o'clock: cloudy)

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
3 Stations by JR Ltd. Express Azusa No. 31

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
Koufu

05:08.260 --> 05:11.950
I was up all night thinking of a route so close to the limits, that if I make all the transfers...

05:11.950 --> 05:13.420
I might barely make it home!!

05:14.210 --> 05:17.330
These people also seem to like limits.

05:19.100 --> 05:21.350
Wanna come...along with me?

05:21.350 --> 05:22.160
Hm...?

05:23.900 --> 05:24.940
<b>Let's go!</b>

05:31.870 --> 05:33.860
He took them with him...

05:34.290 --> 05:37.470
Chitan-kun's love of trains is also pretty troublesome, huh?

05:37.910 --> 05:39.790
You've got that right!

05:39.790 --> 05:42.150
I think there's more wrong with it than that!

06:08.020 --> 06:09.680
Failed Transfer.

06:14.930 --> 06:17.430
Torauma Park

06:25.900 --> 06:27.070
2 - 32

06:27.400 --> 06:30.670
My father's company went bankrupt.

06:31.120 --> 06:33.060
Oh my... that's awful.

06:35.260 --> 06:38.050
Hey, you know what I saw in the park this morning?

06:38.090 --> 06:40.560
There was some man wearing a suit, sitting on a swing the whole time.

06:40.940 --> 06:44.210
It has to be restructuring. I'm sure he can't tell his family!

06:47.280 --> 06:49.720
There are people who can't sense the mood.

06:51.650 --> 06:54.540
It's definitely over there...!

06:54.540 --> 06:55.730
Oh, really?

06:56.990 --> 06:58.450
Oh, Umi-chan.

06:58.450 --> 06:59.880
Ah, Ryō-chan!

06:59.880 --> 07:02.980
Good timing! Do you know the film "Toraumaza"?

07:03.180 --> 07:06.480
I was just on my way there, too!

07:06.480 --> 07:09.490
I love you...

07:16.880 --> 07:18.730
It turned out to be surprisingly funny, huh?

07:19.710 --> 07:21.750
There are people who can't sense the mood.

07:23.880 --> 07:26.460
Hmmm.... ah....really?

07:26.760 --> 07:28.840
And you know what? It's a masterpiece!

07:29.170 --> 07:32.340
Say, Umi-chan, don't you need to take a bath now?

07:32.340 --> 07:35.190
Tomorrow's Love

07:32.670 --> 07:35.100
And now that I think of it, TV dramas are starting up...

07:35.600 --> 07:37.040
Oh, no problem, I've already taken a bath

07:37.040 --> 07:39.100
and I don't watch TV dramas anyway.

07:39.350 --> 07:41.590
There are people who can't sense the mood.

07:42.190 --> 07:45.040
Going Musume

07:45.230 --> 07:47.050
Sciencevestigation Club

07:47.480 --> 07:49.120
It's a serious condition, isn't it.

07:49.220 --> 07:53.040
If you're that bad at sensing mood, you'll never find any friends.

07:53.040 --> 07:54.060
What was that?!

07:54.400 --> 07:57.630
Don't be rude! Of course I can sense mood!!

07:57.950 --> 08:00.000
If she doesn't notice it herself, there's no help for it.

08:00.250 --> 08:02.200
She can't sense the mood anyway.

08:04.070 --> 08:05.100
Now, now...

08:05.100 --> 08:08.100
How about asking a third party?

08:08.090 --> 08:09.620
First Investigation Report
Yamada-san

08:09.930 --> 08:11.330
Huh? Umi-chan?

08:11.860 --> 08:14.250
Oh right, there was something...

08:15.000 --> 08:16.850
20th Torauma Cup

08:15.000 --> 08:16.850
Intra-school Marathon Competition

08:15.060 --> 08:17.140
Back during the school's marathon event...

08:17.600 --> 08:20.760
Our mood was all like "Let's run slowly everybody!"

08:32.490 --> 08:36.950
Oh yeah, that's right. There are people who just care about their solo performance.

08:36.950 --> 08:39.530
Don't tell Umi-chan, or she'll put me on her hate list.

08:39.660 --> 08:41.160
2nd Investigation Report

08:41.160 --> 08:42.540
Huh? Umi-chan?

08:43.400 --> 08:46.150
Now that you mention it, I also remember something like that...

08:46.840 --> 08:49.360
We had a little party at my place.

08:49.880 --> 08:52.500
I win! Okay Umi-chan, that means a Penalty Game for you!

08:53.550 --> 08:54.630
I don't want to.

08:57.660 --> 08:59.340
But...you have to play a Penalty Game now...

08:59.400 --> 09:00.040
I said I don't want to.

09:00.640 --> 09:03.550
Why do I have to do something like that?

09:07.750 --> 09:12.650
Yeah, there are those people who refuse Penalty Games and kill the party.

09:12.650 --> 09:15.280
Don't tell Umi-chan, or she'll put me on her hate list.

09:15.280 --> 09:15.930
Grudge

09:16.030 --> 09:20.670
Can-I-let-this-grudge-go-un-avenged...?!

09:16.030 --> 09:20.670
Grudge Note

09:21.050 --> 09:23.810
There are more names in your hate list now, huh?

09:23.810 --> 09:27.010
Well, well, Umi's inability to sense the mood is really showing itself now.

09:27.250 --> 09:29.920
That's not true, those things just happened by chance!!

09:30.470 --> 09:34.250
If you can't sense the mood, it will also bother other people.

09:34.440 --> 09:37.240
It's not even an exaggeration to call it a crime.

09:37.820 --> 09:39.750
For example, when an elementary school teacher

09:39.750 --> 09:45.070
is completely unable to sense the mood of a child that has to go to the bathroom

09:45.070 --> 09:47.770
imagine what a trauma that will cause!!

09:49.370 --> 09:53.280
Not being able to sense the mood causes terrible situations!

09:53.460 --> 09:55.960
Everything you've been saying is pretty rude!

09:55.960 --> 09:58.000
I can sense the mood if I want to!

09:58.340 --> 10:01.320
Well then- try to sense <i>this</i> mood!

10:02.080 --> 10:05.180
Huh? Distress, maybe?

10:05.180 --> 10:06.720
Bzzzt!! The right answer is...

10:07.370 --> 10:09.720
...your daughter's boyfriend has come to visit you at home

10:09.720 --> 10:12.470
and you're feeling nervous about when he'll ask to marry her.

10:12.780 --> 10:15.060
Nobody would get that one!!

10:15.090 --> 10:17.510
Okay, what about this one?

10:18.430 --> 10:20.070
You've hit a kid that ran into the street

10:20.070 --> 10:23.090
and now you don't know whether you should just leave or call an ambulance?

10:23.420 --> 10:24.420
Bzzt.

10:24.420 --> 10:26.070
The limited edition of a Dating Sim is sold out

10:26.070 --> 10:28.980
so you're all upset and wondering if there still might be one left somewhere.

10:29.020 --> 10:30.810
I have no idea where you got that from!

10:31.360 --> 10:34.010
As expected, you just can't sense the mood at all!

10:35.870 --> 10:38.890
I'm going to achieve the ability to sense the mood!!

10:41.700 --> 10:43.030
Umi trained.

10:44.940 --> 10:47.250
<i>What's with this feeling of uneasiness?</i>

10:48.560 --> 10:49.290
Ron!

10:49.610 --> 10:50.550
Curry?

10:50.550 --> 10:51.670
Or Spaghetti Neapolitan?

10:51.670 --> 10:54.650
Which one will be your order tonight?

10:51.670 --> 10:54.650
Messhu

10:51.670 --> 10:54.650
Hiroshi

10:55.300 --> 10:56.450
I'm going with Messhu's!

10:56.780 --> 10:58.420
She exposed herself to many different situations

10:58.420 --> 11:01.000
so she would become able to sense the mood.

11:01.160 --> 11:03.410
About two meters to the right...

11:04.700 --> 11:05.670
And thus...

11:04.700 --> 11:05.670
Private Torauma High School

11:06.650 --> 11:09.510
She became able to sense the mood.

11:10.010 --> 11:13.750
I feel it perfectly, this mood of tension.

11:13.750 --> 11:16.960
I can sense this mood full of regret.

11:17.090 --> 11:18.900
The elementary schoolchild covered in blood

11:17.650 --> 11:21.160
No, Umi!! A sixth sense is not what you call "sensing the mood"!!

11:18.900 --> 11:20.030
who wants to play with this friends

11:20.030 --> 11:21.200
the soldier covered in bandages...

11:21.390 --> 11:23.080
Sciencevestigation Club

11:23.560 --> 11:26.750
Although I tried so hard and trained so much, it's still wrong...

11:27.150 --> 11:30.180
Well, but it's not like there's no other way.

11:30.650 --> 11:32.710
If you're unable to sense the mood...

11:33.580 --> 11:36.360
Then you can just change the mood itself!!

11:36.690 --> 11:38.880
Change... the mood?

11:39.530 --> 11:41.400
People like the O-some Brothers

11:41.420 --> 11:46.310
Shinohara or Rikiya have the power to change the mood where ever they go.

11:46.830 --> 11:48.310
I... I see...

11:48.640 --> 11:50.660
You have this power as well, Umi!

11:51.880 --> 11:55.100
This heartwarming scene at the park...

11:55.870 --> 11:58.320
Just from you being there, the mood completely changes!

11:58.370 --> 11:58.920
Right?

11:59.030 --> 12:01.740
Why you want to turn me into that kind of character!?

12:01.740 --> 12:05.450
And the ones with the greatest power to change the mood...

12:05.670 --> 12:07.940
Are the Edo Hipsters!

12:07.950 --> 12:10.230
E-Edo Hipsters?

12:20.000 --> 12:23.400
Former Genius Cram School Edo Hipster Course: Maeda-sama.

12:25.810 --> 12:28.840
Ma...Maeda-sama!! You are unconventional as always!!

12:28.840 --> 12:32.980
As expected of someone who obtained the license to be eccentric directly from the Shōgun!

12:33.000 --> 12:35.400
It's going to change, the mood in the city will completely change!

12:35.410 --> 12:36.270
Yeah, it'll definitely change!

12:37.290 --> 12:40.450
For example, this tranquil Sunday...

12:41.530 --> 12:43.910
An Edo Hipster just being there changes the mood completely!

12:44.990 --> 12:47.960
For example, this peaceful, everyday scene...

12:49.030 --> 12:50.910
An Edo Hipster just being there changes the mood completely!

12:51.480 --> 12:53.290
Come on, Umi, be eccentric as well!!

13:03.600 --> 13:06.020
Want to be unconventional, too?

13:12.410 --> 13:13.760
He tried being unconventional.

13:16.600 --> 13:19.820
Give me your pennies!! Give me your pennies!!

13:19.820 --> 13:23.300
Be refined! Be refined!

13:23.300 --> 13:26.810
<i>Dance!! Dance!! Be refined!!</i>

13:25.750 --> 13:27.740
So that's what unconventional means...

13:30.550 --> 13:32.050
He overdid it.

13:46.080 --> 13:47.200
Private Torauma High School

13:48.550 --> 13:52.030
So this... is Torauma High School?

13:52.280 --> 13:55.950
I've finally found it!

13:56.060 --> 13:58.410
Suddenly, a rival appears?!

13:59.300 --> 14:03.740
She's the only one I can never forgive....

14:04.200 --> 14:06.150
Someone from the past?!

14:07.070 --> 14:12.030
This woman is the only one I can never forgive!!

14:12.070 --> 14:16.120
Saien Suzu! Never...!

14:16.910 --> 14:19.920
The Woman from the West

14:22.150 --> 14:24.720
<i>But I must say...according to my investigations</i>

14:25.190 --> 14:29.020
<i>that woman has got some followers that are bad news!</i>

14:29.020 --> 14:30.500
Murdering Back-Stabber

14:29.020 --> 14:30.500
Demonic Railway-Zombie

14:29.020 --> 14:30.500
Anti-Pervert Lethal Weapon

14:30.930 --> 14:33.650
<i>So they will get back at me.</i>

14:33.720 --> 14:36.200
<i>She won't get involved that easily!</i>

14:37.100 --> 14:39.810
Urgently Recruiting Student Council President (due to vacancy)

14:37.600 --> 14:39.560
<i>They're looking for a new student council president?</i>

14:41.000 --> 14:42.000
That's it!

14:42.600 --> 14:44.400
Private Torauma High School

14:54.700 --> 14:56.600
It's so peaceful.

14:58.290 --> 14:59.900
Bad news!!

15:00.920 --> 15:04.410
The Student Council has announced they're cutting our club's budget!

15:04.490 --> 15:06.130
Huh? They're cutting our budget?

15:06.470 --> 15:11.750
That's strange, I've properly talked to each successive Student Council President...

15:13.820 --> 15:15.870
Having them listen to graceful music...

15:17.450 --> 15:20.250
Sharing intimate physical contact with them...

15:21.030 --> 15:24.440
and getting to know each other's favorite things.

15:26.050 --> 15:29.990
Didn't the last president quit from anxiety and free up the position again?

15:30.760 --> 15:35.320
Apparently, an exchange student appeared suddenly and became Student Council President!

15:36.930 --> 15:39.470
Well then, I'll have to speak to that person as well...

15:39.530 --> 15:40.920
You won't!

15:40.940 --> 15:41.370
Who are you?

15:41.750 --> 15:44.300
I'm Nichibe Yoshio, Student Council Secretary!

15:44.300 --> 15:46.850
I'm Kumon Kazuo, Student Council Treasurer!

15:47.730 --> 15:51.660
Up until now, you guys recklessly used up half the whole budget!

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Heisei 10 - Budget

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Sciencevestigation Club

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Club Budget

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Kendō Club

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Soccer Club

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Baseball Club

15:51.020 --> 15:51.680
Tea Ceremony Club

15:51.980 --> 15:53.930
We got that much!?

15:54.040 --> 15:55.760
What the heck did we use it all for?

15:56.380 --> 15:59.340
Well.... for various important things...

15:59.570 --> 16:01.230
However, that has now come to an end!

16:01.560 --> 16:02.850
New President, come on in!!

16:05.560 --> 16:06.710
But there's nobody there.

16:06.900 --> 16:08.790
Hey, that's weird...

16:10.290 --> 16:11.740
I'm already here!

16:22.000 --> 16:24.250
Ba ha ha, did I scare you?!!

16:24.590 --> 16:27.740
In situations like this, you need to make a dramatic entrance!

16:27.770 --> 16:29.860
Your position is finally going to be settled!

16:30.280 --> 16:31.590
I'm sure...

16:31.770 --> 16:34.090
So that's how she got her position?

16:34.450 --> 16:37.580
By the way...who are you?

16:38.870 --> 16:42.130
What are you saying to your eternal rival!?

16:42.130 --> 16:44.430
Stop acting like you don't know me!!

16:44.820 --> 16:47.090
The Chief probably really did forget though.

16:44.940 --> 16:47.300
<i>There's no way you could have forgotten me!</i>

16:47.350 --> 16:48.590
She's like that, isn't she.

16:48.650 --> 16:50.670
<i>Oi, say something!</i>

16:49.410 --> 16:52.430
But what's her relationship to the Chief?

16:52.490 --> 16:55.690
Allow me to explain that!

16:56.700 --> 16:58.540
Principal, what's with that get-up...?

16:58.820 --> 17:00.610
In the east is Suzu from Akiba!

17:00.670 --> 17:02.470
In the west is Jun from Nipponbashi!

17:02.580 --> 17:07.000
The two of them, who were idols to the computer kids, were die-hard rivals!

17:07.880 --> 17:12.260
That these two were put together as a duo caused quite an uproar!

17:07.880 --> 17:12.260
Suzu & Jun "Love is LSI"

17:12.820 --> 17:18.350
I still remember it, their legendary Guerrilla Open-Air Concert in front of Yonohonmachi Station!

17:16.780 --> 17:18.870
Suzu & Jun FC

17:16.780 --> 17:18.870
LSI Addicts

17:18.870 --> 17:20.910
So you were a fan of theirs?!

17:22.910 --> 17:23.840
Did something happen?

17:24.060 --> 17:27.220
For some reason, Chief's self-proclaimed rival showed up.

17:27.470 --> 17:28.690
The Professor's rival?

17:29.740 --> 17:32.700
How totally sneaky, why just the Professor?!

17:32.980 --> 17:36.780
I don't even have a rival yet!! I'll fight you!!

17:40.520 --> 17:42.260
So you're the Professor's rival!?

17:42.830 --> 17:44.980
'Sup with that dangerous-looking guy...

17:48.760 --> 17:51.380
"<b>Sup</b>"? Are you from Kansai maybe?

17:51.380 --> 17:53.160
What's so funny about that?

17:53.980 --> 17:54.910
Well...

17:55.250 --> 17:59.190
You people from Kansai eat rice as a side dish to okonomiyaki, don't you?

18:01.380 --> 18:03.680
Wh-what's wrong with that?

18:03.850 --> 18:06.230
It's totally weird!

18:06.230 --> 18:07.860
It's completely normal.

18:08.020 --> 18:10.800
It's you guys who eat it by itself who are weird!

18:10.900 --> 18:14.470
Eh, but eating carbs with other carbs...

18:15.690 --> 18:19.620
In that case, do you also eat rice as a side dish to takoyaki?

18:19.740 --> 18:20.380
Wha...

18:20.710 --> 18:22.760
Takoyaki is a snack!

18:22.760 --> 18:24.860
Okonomiyaki is a full dish!!

18:24.860 --> 18:27.510
Eh, but they're so similar...!

18:28.660 --> 18:32.010
You've just made everybody in Kansai your enemy!

18:32.010 --> 18:33.040
I'm really pissed now!!

18:33.350 --> 18:37.840
Well, anyway, you have a fatal flaw as a rival.

18:38.000 --> 18:38.970
What...?

18:58.560 --> 19:02.570
There are already lots of strong rivals from Kansai in Shōnen Sunday!

18:58.560 --> 19:02.570
Shōnen Sunday

19:03.000 --> 19:05.880
There's no room left for low-level ones like you!!

19:08.230 --> 19:10.340
Your character overlaps!

19:12.190 --> 19:14.100
W-What do you mean?!

19:21.910 --> 19:24.570
Now, now, fighting is bad.

19:24.580 --> 19:27.920
Don't try and stop me, I'm going to kill him and then kill myself!

19:28.300 --> 19:30.720
Wait, I came to take revenge on <i>you</i>!

19:31.290 --> 19:34.980
But revenge...why do you hate the Chief that much?

19:36.050 --> 19:39.530
Well, it began a long, long time ago...

19:39.650 --> 19:40.760
<i>It's story time.</i>

19:40.830 --> 19:41.800
<i>Let's keep it short, ok?</i>

19:42.000 --> 19:48.760
Our duo's single, "Love is LSI", was a surprise hit even though it was an indie release.

19:49.440 --> 19:50.900
Love is LSI  B Side McDonald's LOVE

19:49.510 --> 19:52.370
I just can't be happy with this split of royalties.

19:50.210 --> 19:52.480
Oricon #1

19:50.910 --> 19:52.510
Guinness Book For Sure

19:51.500 --> 19:52.480
Grammy Nominated

19:51.500 --> 19:52.510
US Billboard No.1

19:51.500 --> 19:52.480
98% of Buyers Pleased

19:51.870 --> 19:52.540
400K Sold Big Hit

19:52.330 --> 19:52.510
No.1 in 50 Countries

19:52.330 --> 19:52.540
Indians Amazed Too

19:52.620 --> 19:54.740
Why was it 7 to 3 in favor of you?!!

19:55.050 --> 19:56.760
That happens a lot in combos!

19:57.140 --> 20:01.000
And then she even shafted me out of my 30%!

20:01.130 --> 20:04.280
Let's open a bank account for the two of us so we'll be safe later.

20:04.630 --> 20:06.410
I really can imagine that...

20:06.690 --> 20:08.090
Give my money back!!

20:08.320 --> 20:11.400
I never realized you were that much of a penny pincher.

20:11.440 --> 20:13.530
<i>Which</i> of us is?! But that's not the only thing!!

20:14.210 --> 20:16.390
When we finally had our major debut...

20:14.210 --> 20:16.390
Love is LSI  B Side McDonald's LOVE

20:14.210 --> 20:16.390
Finally Debut!

20:16.800 --> 20:20.150
As is often is the case, our recording company was worried about our personal safety.

20:20.510 --> 20:23.180
Break off any relationships you're in.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.280
All right.

20:24.600 --> 20:30.300
I tearfully broke up with the beautiful darling I was going out with at the time!

20:30.990 --> 20:34.200
Then I used all my savings and moved to Tokyo.

20:32.100 --> 20:34.040
Big Tokyo of Flowers

20:34.360 --> 20:36.270
And then, when the time for our debut finally had arrived...

20:36.420 --> 20:38.170
I've lost interest. I'm quitting.

20:40.510 --> 20:41.590
See ya...

20:42.360 --> 20:44.510
Can't we just make it a solo act?

20:45.010 --> 20:46.080
Not happening.

20:46.830 --> 20:47.490
Men...

20:47.490 --> 20:48.370
money...

20:48.370 --> 20:49.160
popularity...

20:49.230 --> 20:50.250
my future...

20:50.840 --> 20:53.130
my trust in people...

20:53.190 --> 20:56.550
Suzu took everything I had!

20:57.000 --> 21:00.400
And that's why I will take everything from you, too!!

21:00.510 --> 21:02.130
Who's Suzu's man?

21:02.400 --> 21:03.800
If you mean the Chief's toy...

21:04.800 --> 21:05.940
...that's him.

21:10.610 --> 21:16.000
I'll steal Suzu's most precious man away...

21:16.050 --> 21:20.760
I'll deal with you Osaka-style!

21:24.440 --> 21:25.760
And she did.

21:26.090 --> 21:28.510
H....how cool!!

21:30.860 --> 21:34.690
As my underling, you don't deserve to wear such glorious stripes!!

21:35.100 --> 21:38.770
Apologize to Reinbach! Apologize to Hirata! And to Sano as well!

21:38.770 --> 21:41.430
S-so right now you follow the coolest players

21:41.430 --> 21:45.280
